From: Ophuscado <postbox@ophuscado.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:08:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: Use a 64-bit request bit

The request word is 64 bits wide (readq and writeq), but the entry's bit
was built as 1 << id on an int. From bit 31 that is undefined: on arm64
the shift is taken modulo 32, and 1 << 31 sign-extends to the whole upper
half. On the M2 Ultra, die 0's DISPEXT2 is bit 31 and DISPEXT3 bit 32,
and macOS also sets bits 41, 42 and 45-48 of this word when it starts
the PMP.

Use BIT_ULL, and refuse an entry past the first word, which this driver
does not address.
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
index 8050ade5e..edd2c8d3d 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ static int apple_pmp_report_set_state(struct generic_pm_domain *genpd, bool enab
 {
 	struct apple_pmp_report_entry *ent = genpd_to_apple_pmp_report_entry(genpd);
 	struct apple_pmp_report *rep = dev_get_drvdata(ent->dev->parent);
-	u64 bit_val = 1 << ent->id;
+	u64 bit_val = BIT_ULL(ent->id);
 	u64 val;
 	unsigned long flags;
 
@@ -152,6 +152,8 @@ static int apple_pmp_report_entry_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	ret = of_property_read_u32(node, "reg", &ent->id);
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "missing reg property\n");
+	if (ent->id >= 64)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL, "request bit %u is past the first word\n", ent->id);
 
 	ret = of_property_read_string(node, "label", &name);
 	if (ret < 0)
